WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:07.330
count builds a four-bin histogram with atomics. route scans a selection flag for each category in shared memory.

00:00:07.330 --> 00:00:13.995
Its exclusive prefix gives each token a stable rank; adding the category start gives a unique destination.

00:00:13.995 --> 00:00:19.955
All threads reach every scan barrier, and the histogram producer precedes route in the same stream.

00:00:21.455 --> 00:00:23.140
Count categories.

00:00:23.140 --> 00:00:25.610
Build counts before routing starts.

00:00:25.610 --> 00:00:27.115
Find start and rank.

00:00:27.115 --> 00:00:30.380
Combine the category region and local order.

00:00:30.380 --> 00:00:31.655
Write token ID.

00:00:31.655 --> 00:00:34.190
Give each token a unique stable slot.

00:00:35.690 --> 00:00:39.800
Device-memory phase results connect counting to placement.

00:00:39.800 --> 00:00:46.145
Atomics can count safely, but the order of atomic arrivals alone does not preserve token order.

00:00:46.145 --> 00:00:49.585
The explicit earlier-token rank supplies stability.
